      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-45233",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/34/34c15e6b37e9a4c2a86040ec2a78bf10c844df4128759d7009751cc8239b67f6.png)\n\nWhich of the following combinations of transformations map the polygon $ABCD$ to a congruent polygon?\n\n1. A reflection in the line $AB^(\u27f7)$, followed by a dilation of scale factor $2$ with center of dilation $A$.\n2. A horizontal stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$, followed by a reflection in the axis $AC^(\u27f7)$.\n3. A rotation of $36^{\u2218}$ counterclockwise about the point $A$, followed by a translation of $3$ units to the right and $1$ unit down."
